  "question": {
    "text": "If the line of intersection of the planes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;makes an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;with the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the direction cosines of the line are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The vector along the line of intersection will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>i.e. direction ratios of line are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Direction ratio of normal to&nbsp;the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Since the line makes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;with the plane, so it will make&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;with its normal.</p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msqrt><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msqrt><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p>So, direction ratios of the line&nbsp;can be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp; direction cosines can be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#177;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}